# Mermaid preview in MarkdownEditor

## Problem
Schema docs and other Markdown use ` ```mermaid ` fences with `erDiagram` (and other diagram types). TipTap renders these as plain code blocks — no Mermaid integration exists in the client.

## Approach
1. Add `mermaid`, `@tiptap/extension-code-block-lowlight`, `lowlight`, `prosemirror-mermaid`.
2. Replace StarterKit `codeBlock` with extended `CodeBlockLowlight` + `mermaidPlugin` (stable `id` per block).
3. Initialize Mermaid once with dark theme aligned to app chrome.
4. Style `.mermaid` containers in `index.css`.
5. Remove outdated “may render as code fences” banner text from schema sync script.

## QA follow-up
- First pass used `prosemirror-mermaid` widget decorations alongside `CodeBlockLowlight`; decorations did not surface reliably in the TipTap view.
- Replaced with a React `NodeView` that calls `mermaid.render()` when the editor is in preview/read-only (default for Documents).
- `crypto.randomUUID` unavailable on HTTP LAN dev hosts — added `randomShortId()` fallback for Mermaid block ids.
